{"text": "After analyzing the results, we found that recent developments in contrastive learning for embeddings include applications in unsupervised domain adaptation and invariant rationale discovery. The core concept revolves around using contrastive loss to improve embedding quality by pulling similar samples closer together and pushing dissimilar ones apart. Additionally, there is ongoing research on combining contrastive learning with causal inference from observational data, though specific examples are limited.\n\nTotal number of sources: 10\n\nSummary:\n- Recent applications include unsupervised domain adaptation.\n- Core concept involves improving embedding quality through contrastive loss.\n- Ongoing work combines contrastive learning with causal inference.", "token_logprobs": [-1.6411716938018799, -1.510960578918457, -0.7474328875541687, -1.1208031177520752, -0.37449103593826294, -1.8658788204193115, -0.11170314252376556, -0.26208341121673584, -0.12029492110013962, -0.4839733839035034, -0.011854059062898159, -6.544803909491748e-05, -3.576279254957626e-07, -2.98023678624304e-06, -0.0037329643964767456, -4.2081763240275905e-05, -0.3239218294620514, -0.44263872504234314, -0.02769458293914795, -1.0292471647262573, -3.4570753086882178e-06, 0.0, -0.00014449209265876561, -4.255862222635187e-05, -0.11607853323221207, -0.19606249034404755, -0.01057305745780468, -6.8666908191517e-05, -0.031061427667737007, -1.2253042459487915, -0.4327935576438904, -0.005895374808460474, -0.9737223386764526, -2.2649790025752736e-06, -0.8876203894615173, -0.23946455121040344, -9.536747711536009e-07, -0.20164255797863007, -0.016518859192728996, -0.5780894160270691, -0.38716134428977966, -0.5078555345535278, -1.4642585515975952, -2.211646795272827, -0.002862852066755295, -0.7480269074440002, -0.35903680324554443, -1.6777085065841675, -0.052653782069683075, -0.0033926633186638355, -0.003808409906923771, -2.3842141672503203e-05, -0.1516060084104538, -0.018178666010499, -0.017574902623891